1
00:00:00,940 --> 00:00:03,560
It's been over two months
since our senior year started.

2
00:00:08,670 --> 00:00:09,520
(Watarai: Good morning.)

3
00:00:09,521 --> 00:00:12,010
(Can we walk home together today?)

4
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:19,020
Since retiring from my club, I've been
spending way more time with Watarai.

5
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:24,260
(By the way, I love this photo.
Can I use it as my lock screen?)

6
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:32,319
(Sure.)

7
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:35,229
Lately, I've been walking on air.

8
00:00:35,230 --> 00:00:37,939
- Hioki.
- Morning.

9
00:00:37,940 --> 00:00:39,019
Morning.

10
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:40,040
Morning.

11
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:43,209
What are you grinning about?

12
00:00:43,210 --> 00:00:44,319
Nothing.

13
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:45,290
By the way,

14
00:00:45,291 --> 00:00:47,459
is there something
different about you today?

15
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:49,239
- Oh, a little.
- Your hair?

16
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:51,379
- Oh, you're right.
- I styled it. Does it look weird?

17
00:00:51,380 --> 00:00:53,649
It's not weird at all.

18
00:00:53,650 --> 00:00:55,759
- Just makes me a little emotional.
- Yeah.

19
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:57,839
- Like you're literally glowing.
- Seriously.

20
00:00:57,840 --> 00:01:00,779
Yeah, like—bam, boom, pow!

21
00:01:00,780 --> 00:01:02,439
You're still the same
old you inside, though.

22
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:03,979
That's true.

23
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:05,440
Oh, although...

24
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:07,949
you've gotten a bit more demanding lately.

25
00:01:07,950 --> 00:01:09,059
Oh, I kinda see that.

26
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:11,339
Demanding? What do you mean?

27
00:01:11,340 --> 00:01:12,439
Just little things.

28
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:14,940
Like, "hold this for
me," or "do that for me."

29
00:01:16,110 --> 00:01:17,110
Wait, really?

30
00:01:19,180 --> 00:01:20,479
Actually, yeah.

31
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:22,420
Watarai just spoils me so much,

32
00:01:23,140 --> 00:01:25,450
I guess I've gotten used to it.

33
00:01:28,580 --> 00:01:30,599
Sorry. Is it annoying?

34
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,559
No, no, we don't mind at all!

35
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:33,590
- Not at all.
- Yeah.

36
00:01:34,170 --> 00:01:36,429
Besides, Tsujitani is such a tyrant.

37
00:01:36,430 --> 00:01:38,519
Compared to him, you're a
total walk in the park, Hioki.

38
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:39,550
Right.

39
00:01:43,890 --> 00:01:44,919
See what I mean?

40
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:45,990
Yeah.

41
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:48,419
My tie.

42
00:01:48,420 --> 00:01:49,649
I forgot it.

43
00:01:49,650 --> 00:01:51,079
Someone lend me theirs!

44
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:52,519
Speak of the devil.

45
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:55,239
No one has a spare tie. Just
suck it up and take the lecture.

46
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:56,820
Come on, please!

47
00:01:58,200 --> 00:01:59,200
Hioki!

48
00:02:00,020 --> 00:02:01,030
Help me out here!

49
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:02,939
Just give me half of yours.

50
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:04,959
We'll cut it with scissors.

51
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:06,889
Like splitting an eraser.

52
00:02:06,890 --> 00:02:09,020
Oh, an eraser! Like going halvesies, right?

53
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:12,339
Knock it off! Stop it!

54
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:13,799
My tie... Cut it out!

55
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,210
Tsujitani.

56
00:02:17,540 --> 00:02:19,670
What do you think you're doing to my Hioki?

57
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:21,459
Come on, let's get out of here.

58
00:02:21,460 --> 00:02:23,389
- Watarai's tie...
- Give it up.

59
00:02:23,390 --> 00:02:26,320
He's way out of your league,
man. You don't stand a chance.

60
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:28,600
Morning.

61
00:02:29,230 --> 00:02:30,230
Morning.

62
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:32,560
Oh.

63
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:40,360
There, all fixed.

64
00:02:41,740 --> 00:02:42,740
Thanks.

65
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:45,239
Did you style your hair?

66
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:46,520
Yeah, I used that hair oil.

67
00:02:47,290 --> 00:02:47,860
So cute.

68
00:02:47,861 --> 00:02:49,610
I wore the belt too. Look.

69
00:02:50,210 --> 00:02:52,040
Aw, I'm so glad.

70
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:53,800
It looks great on you.

71
00:02:55,920 --> 00:03:00,070
Oh, sorry, I was just about to text you
back. We can walk home together today.

72
00:03:00,740 --> 00:03:01,540
Okay.

73
00:03:01,541 --> 00:03:03,510
- I'll come get you after school.
- Sounds good.

74
00:03:04,280 --> 00:03:05,280
Oh.

75
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:06,680
I should get going.

76
00:03:08,230 --> 00:03:09,230
Wait.

77
00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:45,220
See you later.

78
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:01,400
I know my head's totally
in the clouds right now.

79
00:04:06,950 --> 00:04:09,910
(Niiyama Suzu: Tsukasa, long time no
see! How are you? How have you been?)

80
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:12,140
But who cares?

81
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:15,859
Because right now,

82
00:04:15,860 --> 00:04:17,670
I'm ridiculously happy.

83
00:05:18,580 --> 00:05:21,940
"School Trip: Joined a Group I'm Not Close to Season2"

84
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:25,463
(Episode 3: After School)
Hioki.

85
00:05:27,180 --> 00:05:28,140
Wanna walk home together?

86
00:05:28,141 --> 00:05:31,639
I'm good. I already made plans
to walk home with Watarai today.

87
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:32,520
Gotcha.

88
00:05:32,521 --> 00:05:34,719
I'll head out then. See you tomorrow.

89
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:36,219
Yeah, see you tomorrow.

90
00:05:36,220 --> 00:05:37,979
- See ya.
- Yeah, see you tomorrow.

91
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:39,210
Well, well.

92
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:41,639
Your skin is glowing. Looking good.

93
00:05:41,640 --> 00:05:43,639
Hioki, are you free today?

94
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:45,059
Wanna hit up the diner with everyone?

95
00:05:45,060 --> 00:05:46,020
Oh, I already have plans with Watarai.

96
00:05:46,021 --> 00:05:47,899
Sweet, then it's practically settled.

97
00:05:47,900 --> 00:05:48,929
I'll go grab him.

98
00:05:48,930 --> 00:05:52,349
Plus, Unscathed Sato is working a
shift today, so you're in for a treat.

99
00:05:52,350 --> 00:05:53,350
Sato?

100
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:55,160
Haven't heard that name in a while.

101
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:01,019
(Watarai: Sorry, something urgent just
came up. I can't walk home with you today.)

102
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:02,790
(I'm really sorry.)

103
00:06:04,340 --> 00:06:06,189
Watarai says he can't make it.

104
00:06:06,190 --> 00:06:07,399
Huh?

105
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:08,529
Why?

106
00:06:08,530 --> 00:06:11,509
Hioki, looks like Watarai already left.

107
00:06:11,510 --> 00:06:12,839
Yeah, he just texted me.

108
00:06:12,840 --> 00:06:14,119
Said something came up.

109
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:15,869
He looked like he was in a
huge rush. What happened?

110
00:06:15,870 --> 00:06:18,119
Not sure, he didn't say.

111
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:19,319
That's rare.

112
00:06:19,320 --> 00:06:22,040
Watarai actually putting
something else before Hioki?

113
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:24,619
Wait, no way! Watarai-kun?

114
00:06:24,620 --> 00:06:25,859
What, what is it?

115
00:06:25,860 --> 00:06:30,359
My friend just saw Watarai
walking home with a super cute girl!

116
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:31,800
What?! No way!

117
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:34,119
Wait, does Watarai have a girlfriend?

118
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:35,098
(Group: Admiring Watarai Tsukasa
from Afar Club (23 members)

119
00:06:35,122 --> 00:06:35,969
*No photos, no stalking.
Accidental sightings only.)

120
00:06:35,970 --> 00:06:37,980
I mean, good for him, I guess...

121
00:06:42,700 --> 00:06:44,600
Wait, what's going on?

122
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:47,480
Who knows? They must've
mistaken him for someone else.

123
00:06:48,580 --> 00:06:49,590
Don't tell me...

124
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:52,580
He's two-timing?

125
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:55,000
No way. He'd never do that.

126
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:56,560
I mean, you say that,

127
00:06:56,561 --> 00:06:58,160
but isn't it super shady?

128
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:00,619
Hioki, you okay?

129
00:07:00,914 --> 00:07:02,079
Is it bothering you?

130
00:07:02,523 --> 00:07:03,989
Oh, no, I'm fine.

131
00:07:04,180 --> 00:07:06,640
I'm sure it's just a misunderstanding too.

132
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:08,509
Let me go ask them.

133
00:07:08,510 --> 00:07:09,960
Wait, you don't have to do that.

134
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:20,059
According to that girl just now,
they're somewhere around here.

135
00:07:20,060 --> 00:07:22,740
Okay, let's go look for them.

136
00:07:23,520 --> 00:07:25,830
Hold on, maybe we should just drop it?

137
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:28,380
But it's gonna eat at
you if we don't, right?

138
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:30,879
We have to get to the bottom of this.

139
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:32,240
But...

140
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:35,940
Let me make one thing clear.

141
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:41,360
Friend or not, cheating is the
one thing I will never forgive.

142
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:43,840
If you don't want to go, Hioki,

143
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:46,080
I'll go check it out myself.

144
00:07:48,460 --> 00:07:49,460
Nakasato...

145
00:07:50,420 --> 00:07:52,979
His ex cheating on him
really scarred him for life.

146
00:07:52,980 --> 00:07:54,759
It's probably nothing.

147
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:56,559
I'm sure they just saw the wrong person.

148
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:58,310
Yeah, I think so too.

149
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,720
Watarai would never do something like that.

150
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:02,400
It's fine.

151
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:04,150
Oh, found him!

152
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:06,160
Let's go.

153
00:08:09,940 --> 00:08:10,920
Come here.

154
00:08:10,921 --> 00:08:12,439
Wait up!

155
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:13,880
Hurry, get over here! Now!

156
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:18,990
What? Where?

157
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:22,600
Look.

158
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:24,080
Right there.

159
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:25,640
Over there.

160
00:08:26,790 --> 00:08:27,790
Watarai!

161
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:33,740
Are you kidding me?

162
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:36,030
Huh?

163
00:08:36,031 --> 00:08:37,859
This is insane.

164
00:08:37,860 --> 00:08:40,600
I'm gonna go throw water in his face.

165
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:42,890
Chill out, man.

166
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:47,620
Wait, I feel like I've
seen that girl before.

167
00:08:55,610 --> 00:08:56,910
Aha, found it.

168
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:01,200
Look at this.

169
00:09:01,820 --> 00:09:02,620
I knew it.

170
00:09:02,621 --> 00:09:03,759
It's her.

171
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:04,760
Look.

172
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:07,460
Oh, I've seen this too.

173
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:08,850
If I remember right...

174
00:09:08,851 --> 00:09:10,239
Oh.

175
00:09:10,240 --> 00:09:11,550
Watarai's ex-girlfriend?

176
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:25,999
What do we do? Should we barge in?

177
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,310
Hold on.

178
00:09:28,460 --> 00:09:31,219
If she's his ex, maybe
they're just friends now.

179
00:09:31,220 --> 00:09:33,189
There might be more to the story.

180
00:09:33,190 --> 00:09:34,899
Yeah.

181
00:09:34,900 --> 00:09:36,239
That's true.

182
00:09:36,240 --> 00:09:37,919
Fair point.

183
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:41,180
Knowing Watarai, I'm
sure he'll explain everything.

184
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:46,139
Are you sure you're okay?

185
00:09:46,140 --> 00:09:49,280
Yeah, I'm fine.

186
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:55,459
Even though I said that...

187
00:09:55,460 --> 00:10:00,540
(The next morning...)

188
00:10:02,100 --> 00:10:03,720
I might not be okay at all.

189
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,880
Seriously, what's the deal with his ex?

190
00:10:10,020 --> 00:10:11,459
Why? What's going on?

191
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:12,440
I don't get it at all.

192
00:10:12,441 --> 00:10:14,980
Ugh, I can't take it anymore.
It's driving me crazy!

193
00:10:15,900 --> 00:10:17,639
- Hioki.
- Yes!

194
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:19,119
Why are you trying to blend into the wall?

195
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:20,200
You doing okay?

196
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:22,220
I'm totally fine.

197
00:10:23,490 --> 00:10:24,370
Are you sure?

198
00:10:24,371 --> 00:10:25,550
Hioki.

199
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:27,120
Morning.

200
00:10:28,280 --> 00:10:29,330
Morning.

201
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:31,919
Oh, sorry about yesterday.

202
00:10:31,920 --> 00:10:33,419
Were you okay walking home by yourself?

203
00:10:33,420 --> 00:10:35,730
Oh, yeah. I walked back with the guys.

204
00:10:36,420 --> 00:10:37,420
I see.

205
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:42,919
Are you okay, Watarai?

206
00:10:42,920 --> 00:10:44,660
I mean, with your situation?

207
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:53,200
Hioki.

208
00:10:57,900 --> 00:11:00,200
Are you free after school today?

209
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:05,520
Yeah.

210
00:11:07,520 --> 00:11:09,080
Let's walk home together, then.

211
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:13,090
There's something I
want to talk to you about.

212
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:29,499
I still wish I could be that book.

213
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:30,460
I'd rather be his headphones.

214
00:11:30,461 --> 00:11:32,800
No way, definitely the book.

215
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:37,900
What does he want to talk about?

216
00:11:45,400 --> 00:11:48,839
Watarai-kun, could you
help me with this problem?

217
00:11:48,840 --> 00:11:51,080
Sure, this part uses the new vocabulary...

218
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:55,060
Come to think of it, I haven't
really heard much about it.

219
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:02,130
What were Watarai's
past relationships like?

220
00:12:02,930 --> 00:12:06,509
That makes so much sense now. Thanks!

221
00:12:06,510 --> 00:12:07,510
Keep at it.

222
00:12:14,060 --> 00:12:15,199
- Hioki.
- Hey.

223
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:17,959
So, how did it go? Did you guys talk?

224
00:12:17,960 --> 00:12:19,279
Not yet.

225
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:20,739
We're going to talk after school.

226
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:22,320
I see.

227
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:23,910
Um...

228
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:27,839
Can I ask you something?

229
00:12:27,840 --> 00:12:29,040
Yeah.

230
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:34,940
Well...

231
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:40,130
Do you know why Watarai
broke up with his ex-girlfriend?

232
00:12:41,970 --> 00:12:45,010
Well, I didn't really ask for the details.

233
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:47,400
But I heard Watarai was
the one who ended it.

234
00:12:47,890 --> 00:12:48,890
Really?

235
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:52,040
Apparently, after starting high school,

236
00:12:55,570 --> 00:12:57,640
her personality suddenly changed.

237
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:00,110
- Her personality?
- Yeah.

238
00:13:00,820 --> 00:13:04,279
So his feelings for her just faded away.

239
00:13:04,280 --> 00:13:06,520
I think that was the reason.

240
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:10,119
My personality hasn't changed, though.

241
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:11,699
That's true.

242
00:13:11,700 --> 00:13:13,220
Still...

243
00:13:14,220 --> 00:13:15,860
I've gotten more needy than I used to be.

244
00:13:18,020 --> 00:13:19,020
Wait, could it be...

245
00:13:20,160 --> 00:13:21,460
What's wrong?

246
00:13:24,150 --> 00:13:27,740
Did Watarai lose interest in
me because I got too needy?

247
00:13:34,180 --> 00:13:35,480
See you later.

248
00:13:54,920 --> 00:13:56,219
So...

249
00:13:56,220 --> 00:13:58,640
About what I wanted
to tell you this morning...

250
00:13:59,750 --> 00:14:00,750
Yeah.

251
00:14:03,450 --> 00:14:04,980
Actually...

252
00:14:07,840 --> 00:14:10,160
There's a favor I want to ask you, Hioki.

253
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:16,339
Honestly,

254
00:14:16,340 --> 00:14:18,360
I didn't want to bring this up at all.

255
00:14:20,970 --> 00:14:23,420
This heavy mood... I knew it.

256
00:14:28,150 --> 00:14:29,340
I'm sorry, Hioki.

257
00:14:31,730 --> 00:14:33,140
I...

258
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,430
Don't tell me...

259
00:14:41,630 --> 00:14:42,920
I...

260
00:14:47,170 --> 00:14:48,570
Am I getting dumped?

261
00:14:53,820 --> 00:14:56,643
I want you to come with me
to meet my ex-girlfriend.

262
00:15:00,670 --> 00:15:01,670
Huh?

263
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:18,580
Sorry for asking something
so weird out of nowhere.

264
00:15:20,700 --> 00:15:22,740
Actually, right after our last date,

265
00:15:23,360 --> 00:15:26,150
I ran into my ex-girlfriend.

266
00:15:27,820 --> 00:15:29,459
I knew it was you, Tsukasa.

267
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:31,079
Are you by yourself right now?

268
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:32,339
If you're free, maybe we
could grab a coffee and talk...

269
00:15:32,340 --> 00:15:33,340
Sorry.

270
00:15:33,820 --> 00:15:35,260
My bus is almost here.

271
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:37,500
Oh, okay.

272
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:40,500
Then...

273
00:15:41,640 --> 00:15:43,100
I'll text you later.

274
00:15:44,170 --> 00:15:45,170
Huh?

275
00:15:49,120 --> 00:15:50,419
After that,

276
00:15:50,420 --> 00:15:53,560
she reached out saying she wanted to talk.

277
00:15:54,660 --> 00:15:55,959
But

278
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:58,120
I didn't want to make you worry,

279
00:15:58,920 --> 00:16:00,240
so I turned her down at first.

280
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:04,930
And then yesterday...

281
00:16:14,510 --> 00:16:16,510
(Sorry, I really want to talk to you.)

282
00:16:17,050 --> 00:16:18,929
(Even five minutes is
fine. Can we meet up?)

283
00:16:18,930 --> 00:16:21,390
(I'm near your school
right now, Tsukasa...)

284
00:16:23,680 --> 00:16:25,760
I couldn't just leave her hanging.

285
00:16:30,180 --> 00:16:32,940
- Cafe latte, right?
- Yeah.

286
00:16:35,990 --> 00:16:36,990
Here you go.

287
00:16:37,770 --> 00:16:39,059
Thanks.

288
00:16:39,060 --> 00:16:40,740
You still remember.

289
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:44,119
So, how have you been lately?

290
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:45,509
Is high school fun?

291
00:16:45,510 --> 00:16:47,620
Yeah, it's great.

292
00:16:48,210 --> 00:16:49,589
It's co-ed, right?

293
00:16:49,590 --> 00:16:52,490
I bet you're super popular.

294
00:16:54,900 --> 00:16:56,200
Suzu.

295
00:16:57,640 --> 00:16:58,989
What did you want to talk about?

296
00:16:58,990 --> 00:17:00,819
Oh, sorry.

297
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:02,540
Well...

298
00:17:03,950 --> 00:17:06,730
Do you have a girlfriend
right now, Tsukasa?

299
00:17:10,100 --> 00:17:11,600
I am seeing

300
00:17:12,260 --> 00:17:13,560
someone.

301
00:17:14,930 --> 00:17:16,350
From your school?

302
00:17:17,080 --> 00:17:17,980
Yeah.

303
00:17:17,981 --> 00:17:19,119
What are they like?

304
00:17:19,120 --> 00:17:20,500
Do you have a picture?

305
00:17:29,540 --> 00:17:30,840
Why are you hiding them?

306
00:17:31,820 --> 00:17:33,339
I'm not hiding them...

307
00:17:33,340 --> 00:17:35,150
Then just let me see.

308
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:37,830
- No.
- Why not?

309
00:17:41,720 --> 00:17:43,020
I get it.

310
00:17:43,870 --> 00:17:45,590
You're not actually seeing anyone, are you?

311
00:17:45,980 --> 00:17:46,850
Huh?

312
00:17:46,851 --> 00:17:49,880
Because there isn't a single
photo on your Instagram.

313
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:52,940
Look, I'm not showing you any pictures.

314
00:17:53,460 --> 00:17:54,900
If that's all you wanted to say,

315
00:17:55,460 --> 00:17:56,760
I'm leaving.

316
00:18:01,540 --> 00:18:02,540
Bye.

317
00:18:03,660 --> 00:18:04,950
I want to move on.

318
00:18:08,220 --> 00:18:09,620
I still like you.

319
00:18:10,320 --> 00:18:11,880
I still have feelings for you, Tsukasa.

320
00:18:13,900 --> 00:18:15,200
That's why.

321
00:18:15,940 --> 00:18:17,760
I need closure so I can finally give up.

322
00:18:19,160 --> 00:18:20,460
If you won't show me a photo,

323
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:22,360
can I at least meet her?

324
00:18:27,690 --> 00:18:29,090
Are you serious?

325
00:18:30,420 --> 00:18:31,719
Please.

326
00:18:31,720 --> 00:18:33,520
I want to move forward.

327
00:18:39,580 --> 00:18:40,879
I'm sorry.

328
00:18:40,880 --> 00:18:43,540
I should've just shut her down completely.

329
00:18:45,020 --> 00:18:46,320
No,

330
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,370
you don't need to apologize.

331
00:18:51,080 --> 00:18:52,380
Besides,

332
00:18:53,450 --> 00:18:54,490
I owe you an apology, too.

333
00:18:55,760 --> 00:18:56,760
Huh?

334
00:19:00,290 --> 00:19:02,060
Actually, yesterday,

335
00:19:03,620 --> 00:19:06,059
I followed you and saw everything.

336
00:19:06,060 --> 00:19:08,500
I saw you with Suzu-san.

337
00:19:10,760 --> 00:19:12,080
You saw us?

338
00:19:12,940 --> 00:19:13,940
I'm sorry.

339
00:19:19,190 --> 00:19:20,540
Wait...

340
00:19:22,580 --> 00:19:23,879
Did I

341
00:19:23,880 --> 00:19:25,960
make you feel insecure?

342
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:31,410
Yeah, a little.

343
00:19:35,300 --> 00:19:36,600
I'm so sorry.

344
00:19:37,320 --> 00:19:38,620
That's completely my fault.

345
00:19:41,120 --> 00:19:43,520
No, it's not your fault.

346
00:19:44,740 --> 00:19:46,840
I was just overthinking things.

347
00:19:48,420 --> 00:19:51,740
I even thought you might dump me.

348
00:19:55,980 --> 00:19:57,279
I'd never do that.

349
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:58,650
Never in a million years.

350
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:06,260
I only have eyes for you, Hioki.

351
00:20:07,980 --> 00:20:09,280
From now on, too.

352
00:20:10,140 --> 00:20:12,700
I'm never letting you
go for the rest of my life.

353
00:20:22,080 --> 00:20:23,480
Thank goodness.

354
00:20:26,880 --> 00:20:28,179
Feel better now?

355
00:20:28,180 --> 00:20:29,350
Yeah.

356
00:20:32,960 --> 00:20:34,360
But is it really okay,

357
00:20:35,820 --> 00:20:36,859
Hmm?

358
00:20:36,860 --> 00:20:38,740
for me to actually meet her?

359
00:20:41,366 --> 00:20:43,346
Now that I think about it, yeah.

360
00:20:44,780 --> 00:20:46,740
I kind of blurted that
out on impulse earlier.

361
00:20:47,980 --> 00:20:50,560
We should really think
through what the best option is.

362
00:20:51,610 --> 00:20:54,060
Yeah, let's figure it out together.

363
00:20:55,330 --> 00:20:57,330
- Thanks.
- Yeah.

364
00:21:01,420 --> 00:21:02,720
Well then,

365
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:05,640
want to head to my place
now for a strategy meeting?

366
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:08,000
Wait, your place?

367
00:21:08,001 --> 00:21:09,119
Your house, Watarai?

368
00:21:09,120 --> 00:21:10,439
Yeah.

369
00:21:10,440 --> 00:21:11,640
After all,

370
00:21:12,240 --> 00:21:15,700
it's better to talk about
this somewhere private.

371
00:21:16,220 --> 00:21:17,519
But

372
00:21:17,520 --> 00:21:20,069
is it okay for me to just
drop by unannounced?

373
00:21:20,070 --> 00:21:21,189
Yeah.

374
00:21:21,190 --> 00:21:22,900
Nobody's home today anyway.

375
00:21:26,110 --> 00:21:27,509
Nobody's home?

376
00:21:27,510 --> 00:21:29,120
So,

377
00:21:29,660 --> 00:21:31,340
if it works for you,

378
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:33,900
do you want to come over?

379
00:21:42,260 --> 00:21:44,380
Whoa, it's pouring.

380
00:21:52,430 --> 00:21:54,239
- Come on in.
- Oh, thanks.

381
00:21:54,240 --> 00:21:56,700
- I'll go grab some towels.
- Oh, okay.

382
00:22:00,600 --> 00:22:02,360
I really came over.

383
00:22:03,120 --> 00:22:08,120
We're just here to talk. There's
no reason to be this nervous.

384
00:22:09,030 --> 00:22:10,699
Still...

385
00:22:10,700 --> 00:22:13,200
- Sorry to keep you waiting.
- It's fine.

386
00:22:15,590 --> 00:22:16,590
Thanks.

387
00:22:37,510 --> 00:22:40,069
Hioki, what are you doing?

388
00:22:40,070 --> 00:22:41,060
Come on in.

389
00:22:41,061 --> 00:22:43,990
Oh, excuse me.

390
00:22:46,440 --> 00:22:47,899
At Watarai's house,

391
00:22:47,900 --> 00:22:49,380
all alone together...

392
00:22:50,530 --> 00:22:52,260
Am I going to survive this?

393
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,479
(Next Episode Preview)
Awesome!

394
00:22:57,480 --> 00:22:59,600
(First Visit to My Boyfriend's House)
That's not fair.

395
00:23:00,660 --> 00:23:02,579
Something I haven't even told my family...

396
00:23:02,580 --> 00:23:05,919
Have you ever thought
about doing it with me?

397
00:23:05,920 --> 00:23:07,899
About Watarai's ex-girlfriend...

398
00:23:07,900 --> 00:23:11,019
I really do want to stay by Watarai's side.

399
00:23:11,020 --> 00:23:12,760
Please go out with me.

400
00:23:15,020 --> 00:23:16,030
It's okay.
